      "@type": "https://litlfred.github.io/bootstrap/v0/ns#Process",
      "name": "QA report signing",
      "summary": "Attesting a QA report: build the test run, work out what the performer can actually reach, and sign — over the API where that is available, or as release authority where it is not.",
      "description": "Attesting a QA report: build the test run, work out what the performer can actually reach, and sign — over the API where that is available, or as release authority where it is not.\n\nYou are in this process when a report needs to become evidence somebody else can rely on. The reach resolution before the gateway is the point: the route is CHOSEN from what the signer can do, not assumed, and the process records which route signed it so a reader of the attestation can tell.\n\nA signature whose route is unrecorded is a signature whose weight cannot be judged later, which is why that step is drawn rather than left implicit.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "sourcePath": "processes/sdlc/qa-report-signing.bpmn",
